1
00:01:50,436 --> 00:01:52,436


2
00:01:56,779 --> 00:01:57,425
Hang in there!

3
00:01:57,449 --> 00:01:59,440
We'll soon reach the hill overlooking my castle!

4
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:00,780
Keep up! Don't fall behind!

5
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:02,760
All right!

6
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:12,018
Oh no!

7
00:02:12,476 --> 00:02:13,980
The town of Goldland is on fire!

8
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:15,680
What could have happened?

9
00:02:20,330 --> 00:02:21,698
Anyway, I'm going to check it out.

10
00:02:22,095 --> 00:02:23,520
You go straight home.

11
00:02:25,304 --> 00:02:27,940
Maybe I can help too, Franz.

12
00:02:28,744 --> 00:02:31,740
Nonsense, a little fire like that is nothing. I can handle it alone.

13
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:36,480
Now, don't follow me. Goodbye.

14
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,720
<i>I wonder if Franz will be okay by himself.</i>

15
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:45,400
<i>I went to help, but Franz stopped me...</i>

16
00:02:46,016 --> 00:02:47,430
<i>I'm really worried.</i>

17
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:50,100
<i>I know, let me sneak over and take a look.</i>

18
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:55,180
Opal, keep watch for me!

19
00:03:22,650 --> 00:03:25,500
Oh no! The Ribbon Knight set the fire!

20
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:29,573
The fire was set by the Ribbon Knight!

21
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,220
It's the Ribbon's Knight!

22
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:34,900
It's the Ribbon!

23
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:35,720
Who set it?

24
00:03:35,945 --> 00:03:36,945
It was the Ribbon!

25
00:03:02,546 --> 00:03:04,220
Help me!

26
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,460
Help me!

27
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,340
What on earth happened? What's with this fire?

28
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:54,960
Forgive me, Your Highness, but Ribbon Knight is the one who set this fire!

29
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:56,700
The Ribbon Knight?

30
00:03:57,503 --> 00:03:59,776
<i>Something's off about the Ribbon Knight...</i>

31
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:08,480
Come on, leave this to us and evacuate to safety!

32
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:18,113
Hurry, we have to stop the fire from spreading!

33
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,000
Prince Franz!

34
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:24,540
It's the Ribbon Knight!

35
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:25,853
Hold it!

36
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,400
Curse you, Ribbon Knight!

37
00:04:28,290 --> 00:04:29,960
Help!

38
00:04:31,589 --> 00:04:34,099
Help me! I'm scared!

39
00:04:34,719 --> 00:04:35,860
Help!

40
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,440
That was close!

41
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:42,720
You're safe now!

42
00:04:42,805 --> 00:04:43,805
Ribbon Knight!

43
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:46,080
I knew it was you!

44
00:04:47,655 --> 00:04:51,420
How dare you show your face before me!

45
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:53,973
What? What's wrong with you, Prince Franz?!

46
00:04:54,535 --> 00:04:57,386
Don't play dumb! You set this fire, didn't you?!

47
00:04:59,290 --> 00:05:00,900
Me? Set a fire...?

48
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:03,013
Still playing innocent?!

49
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:06,146
I won't let you get away with this today! Prepare yourself!

50
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:09,326
Wait! This must be some kind of misunderstanding!

51
00:05:10,290 --> 00:05:11,780
Silence! Talk is useless!

52
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:21,620
Wait, Prince Franz! Saving this child comes first!

53
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:26,720
Come on, hurry, Prince Franz!

54
00:05:28,619 --> 00:05:30,976
The poor thing fainted...

55
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,242
Prince Franz! We can talk later...

56
00:05:34,259 --> 00:05:34,721
 Wait!

57
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:36,640
Damn it!

58
00:06:00,330 --> 00:06:04,080
My darling children have returned.

59
00:06:05,925 --> 00:06:10,400
There, there. I'll give you a special feast.

60
00:06:12,570 --> 00:06:17,159
Look, it's night-bug and honey soup!

61
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:18,773
Come on, eat up!

62
00:06:24,766 --> 00:06:25,560
Who's there?

63
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:29,673
Look out! It's the Ribbon Knight!

64
00:06:30,285 --> 00:06:31,486
Oh my goodness!

65
00:06:31,999 --> 00:06:34,296
You big blabbermouth!

66
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:37,420
Stop shouting Ribbon, Ribbon so loudly, you fool!

67
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:41,533
But old hag! You said the Ribbon Knight set the fire!

68
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:44,720
You were the one who told us to yell out loud, right?!

69
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:47,016
That was in town for everyone to hear!

70
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,749
Here, keep it down and whisper!

71
00:06:48,893 --> 00:06:49,913
By the way, how did it go?

72
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:55,360
Speak louder and clearly!

73
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:57,793
But you just told us to whisper!

74
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:00,213
You both are complete fools!

75
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:04,120
You made Prince Franz believe the Ribbon Knight set the fire, right?

76
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:09,060
So can we have that reward feast now?

77
00:07:09,165 --> 00:07:10,460
We're starving!

78
00:07:10,499 --> 00:07:13,220
Not yet! That's nowhere near enough!

79
00:07:13,295 --> 00:07:14,466
I've had enough of this!

80
00:07:14,625 --> 00:07:16,993
I hate these cramped things!

81
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:19,435
Is that so?

82
00:07:19,673 --> 00:07:23,140
If you refuse to listen to me...

83
00:07:26,759 --> 00:07:30,293
...I can always stick this onto you instead.

84
00:07:30,318 --> 00:07:31,480
No, no, no, no!

85
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:34,313
We'll do whatever you say!

86
00:07:34,625 --> 00:07:36,040
Not that again!

87
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:37,880
We don't want that either!

88
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:41,136
Sora no yo ni osoroshiku,
- Show them something frightening and eerie,

89
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:44,940
odoro-odoroshii omise.
- like the dark sky.

90
00:07:46,653 --> 00:07:48,529
Sora, sora,
-Sky, sky... 

91
00:07:48,553 --> 00:07:52,639
tanashi yume no sekai he ikun jo!
-off to a wonderful dream world you go!

92
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:01,600
Omaetachi ike! Gorudo randojo e!
-Move it, you guys! To Goldland Castle!

93
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:05,157
Soshite Furansu no heya ni aru homotsu
-And fetch the Prince's treasured sword

94
00:08:05,181 --> 00:08:08,580
no oji no ken o totte kurunja !
- from Franz's room!

95
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:13,180
Go! Hurry up!

96
00:08:14,155 --> 00:08:15,155
Yes.

97
00:08:37,249 --> 00:08:38,900
Has something happened to Franz?

98
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:04,700
Hey, it looks like it's in there!

99
00:09:10,679 --> 00:09:13,749
You idiot, he's high-class, so we have to be quiet.

100
00:09:13,773 --> 00:09:14,865
Right, right.

101
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:24,100
Oh, what? It's just a suit of armor.

102
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:25,580
Oh no!

103
00:09:28,189 --> 00:09:31,260
That noise definitely came from this room.

104
00:09:35,039 --> 00:09:37,060
What, it's just a cat and mouse.

105
00:09:43,670 --> 00:09:45,996
If we take this back to the old lady,

106
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:48,700
she'll give us a huge feast!

107
00:10:17,869 --> 00:10:19,466
Oh no! The Prince's sword...

108
00:10:20,989 --> 00:10:23,420
<i>The Prince's sword is mine. — Ribbon Knight.</i>

109
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:26,220
Damn it!

110
00:10:27,199 --> 00:10:29,579
How dare you make me angry! Curse you, Ribbon Knight!

111
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:33,619
What?!

112
00:10:34,259 --> 00:10:36,480
Franz! It's me! Sapphire!

113
00:10:37,413 --> 00:10:38,033
Sapphire?

114
00:10:41,569 --> 00:10:42,766
Hi, Franz!

115
00:10:43,489 --> 00:10:45,240
Sapphire! I told you not to come!

116
00:10:45,759 --> 00:10:49,533
But the fire's still burning, even though it's night. Is something wrong?

117
00:10:50,826 --> 00:10:52,036
Something's wrong, all right!

118
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:54,162
The Ribbon Knight set fire to the castle town,

119
00:10:54,186 --> 00:10:56,435
made innocent people suffer,

120
00:10:56,459 --> 00:10:59,160
and even stole my precious prince's sword!

121
00:11:00,249 --> 00:11:02,182
The Ribbon Knight? No way...

122
00:11:02,733 --> 00:11:04,636
I couldn't believe it at first either.

123
00:11:04,933 --> 00:11:06,649
But I saw him fleeing the fire,

124
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:08,940
and this note is further proof!

125
00:11:12,749 --> 00:11:15,446
<i>That's strange... Who could have done this?</i>

126
00:11:16,699 --> 00:11:19,300
Do you still say it wasn't the Ribbon Knight's doing?

127
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:22,955
But maybe it's someone else's plot...

128
00:11:22,979 --> 00:11:24,069
Enough!

129
00:11:24,753 --> 00:11:26,520
Stop meddling in this!

130
00:11:27,199 --> 00:11:28,042
But, Franz...

131
00:11:28,066 --> 00:11:29,161
I don't want to hear it!

132
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:31,306
Leave!

133
00:11:35,185 --> 00:11:36,185
Just leave!

134
00:11:38,069 --> 00:11:40,500
Franz, let's talk again when you've calmed down.

135
00:11:41,599 --> 00:11:42,239
Goodbye.

136
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,360
<i>Sapphire...</i>

137
00:11:55,899 --> 00:11:57,900
I ended up making Franz angry.

138
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,620
Franz, I'm sorry.

139
00:12:09,969 --> 00:12:10,969
Here she comes.

140
00:12:11,995 --> 00:12:15,273
We can't let her get through.

141
00:12:28,819 --> 00:12:30,260
Opal! Run!

142
00:12:41,849 --> 00:12:43,900
My poor children...

143
00:12:44,049 --> 00:12:46,289
Now that it's come to this,

144
00:12:46,853 --> 00:12:48,000
take this!

145
00:12:55,939 --> 00:13:00,480
Omae wa korekara yume no sekai e iku nda.
-You're going to the dream world now.

146
00:13:04,479 --> 00:13:05,720
My head is spinning!

147
00:13:28,049 --> 00:13:31,580
Sapphire, please forgive me for the awful things I said last night.

148
00:13:36,769 --> 00:13:37,460
An arrow message!

149
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:43,360
<i>Duel location: Today at sunset, waiting by the forest spring. —Ribbon Knight</i>

150
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:48,280
What an impudent Ribbon Knight!

151
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,040
So many moths...

152
00:13:56,643 --> 00:13:58,980
Where on earth... am I?

153
00:14:01,889 --> 00:14:03,900
How did I end up in a place like this?

154
00:14:10,599 --> 00:14:13,180
I see! So this is the fake Ribbon Knight's hideout!

155
00:14:15,506 --> 00:14:16,366
Someone's coming!

156
00:14:31,733 --> 00:14:33,680
Time to eat.

157
00:14:34,229 --> 00:14:35,229
I'm hungry.

158
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:40,793
Not yet! Go back to the swamp and fetch more glow-worms!

159
00:14:43,046 --> 00:14:44,273
What a pain!

160
00:14:45,699 --> 00:14:47,840
Why haven't you left yet?

161
00:14:48,135 --> 00:14:51,480
Because I'm starving. I can't even move anymore.

162
00:14:51,773 --> 00:14:56,980
Then can I put this on your faces and bodies?

163
00:14:56,981 --> 00:14:59,560
Fine, we'll just go, alright?!

164
00:15:02,029 --> 00:15:04,800
She's sleeping soundly, completely unaware.

165
00:15:07,159 --> 00:15:10,320
Now then, change into Ribbon Knight's clothes.

166
00:15:14,568 --> 00:15:16,573
Damn it! The spell wore off!

167
00:15:17,215 --> 00:15:20,700
So you're the one doing evil with a fake Ribbon Knight!

168
00:15:22,404 --> 00:15:26,080
This time, I'll turn <i>you</i> into the fake Ribbon Knight!

169
00:15:42,089 --> 00:15:44,660
Did you really think I'd let you escape so easily?

170
00:15:45,659 --> 00:15:47,920
How's that? You can't even move anymore.

171
00:15:48,135 --> 00:15:51,854
Wait here. In the meantime, I'll bring Franz over.

172
00:15:52,593 --> 00:15:53,406
Franz?

173
00:15:54,179 --> 00:15:58,400
Come, my sweet children, follow me!

174
00:15:59,259 --> 00:16:02,495
They're plotting something again.

175
00:16:03,293 --> 00:16:05,206
I have to warn Franz right away...

176
00:16:10,929 --> 00:16:11,869
Franz!

177
00:16:12,266 --> 00:16:12,922
Franz!

178
00:16:13,293 --> 00:16:14,553
Don't come here!

179
00:16:33,229 --> 00:16:36,442
He's late! After sending me a challenge to a duel!

180
00:16:36,466 --> 00:16:37,779
Curse that Ribbon Knight!

181
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:40,580
Damn it!

182
00:16:56,843 --> 00:16:57,600
Who goes there?

183
00:16:58,806 --> 00:17:01,848
Furansu ojiyo, Ribon no kishi wa
- Prince Franz, that cowardly Ribbon Knight

184
00:17:01,873 --> 00:17:03,666
hikyo ni mo yattekonai.
- isn't going to show up.

185
00:17:03,995 --> 00:17:05,802
Wasu ga Ribon no Kishi
- I shall take you to

186
00:17:05,839 --> 00:17:08,193
no sumika e tsuretetteyaro.
- the Ribbon Knight's lair.

187
00:17:10,249 --> 00:17:12,200
My head is spinning...

188
00:17:12,549 --> 00:17:15,829
Izumi o fukaku chi ni sakanake,
- Springs, tear deep into the earth! 

189
00:17:15,853 --> 00:17:18,747
honoyo takaku ten o kogase,
- Flames, burn high and scorch the heavens!

190
00:17:18,771 --> 00:17:21,833
soshite watashi no kawai kodomotachiyo
- And my sweet children, dance and

191
00:17:21,858 --> 00:17:25,399
odotte konoyo no saigo o iwau noja.
- celebrate the end of this world!

192
00:17:39,899 --> 00:17:47,660
Franz, go to the watermill in the forest. And kill that wretched Ribbon Knight.

193
00:17:49,309 --> 00:17:51,060
Curse that Ribbon Knight...

194
00:18:04,086 --> 00:18:07,752
No matter how much you struggle, you'll never escape that hag.

195
00:18:07,776 --> 00:18:09,906
She's terrifying.

196
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:11,033
Cowards!

197
00:18:11,644 --> 00:18:15,759
What?! Don't you feel pathetic being bossed around by an old hag like that?

198
00:18:17,439 --> 00:18:19,959
We've tried to escape plenty of times,

199
00:18:19,983 --> 00:18:22,312
but she casts strange spells on us every time.

200
00:18:22,336 --> 00:18:25,873
 So let's team up and defeat that hag!

201
00:18:28,149 --> 00:18:29,706
If you untie these ropes,

202
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:31,606
I'll beat the hag myself.

203
00:18:31,630 --> 00:18:34,240
You two run away while I do. How about it?

204
00:18:38,919 --> 00:18:40,193
I'm gonna do it!

205
00:18:40,669 --> 00:18:42,360
I'm gonna do it too!

206
00:18:42,469 --> 00:18:45,040
It's Obaba!

207
00:18:46,986 --> 00:18:48,240
It was only for a little bit...

208
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:54,480
Franz!

209
00:18:56,009 --> 00:19:01,320
Franz, tear this Ribbon Knight to pieces with your sword! Quickly!

210
00:19:04,929 --> 00:19:06,120
You wretched Ribbon Knight!

211
00:19:08,829 --> 00:19:09,658
Franz!

212
00:19:09,949 --> 00:19:10,666
Damn you!

213
00:19:20,293 --> 00:19:21,526
Franz! Are you okay?

214
00:19:26,269 --> 00:19:27,800
Wait... Sapphire?!

215
00:19:27,905 --> 00:19:28,905
What on earth...?

216
00:19:30,529 --> 00:19:31,783
Give me a break...

217
00:19:32,076 --> 00:19:33,850
You were just trying to kill me!

218
00:19:33,875 --> 00:19:34,861
What? You?

219
00:19:35,269 --> 00:19:37,460
That old hag put a spell on you.

220
00:19:38,009 --> 00:19:40,986
And she used a fake Ribbon Knight to torment you.

221
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:47,435
What's this?

222
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:48,460
Franz!

223
00:19:58,069 --> 00:19:59,569


224
00:20:02,639 --> 00:20:03,638
Hold on!

225
00:20:03,669 --> 00:20:04,779
Running scared, are you?!

226
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:36,966
The ceiling...

227
00:20:38,619 --> 00:20:40,900
Franz! The door won't open!

228
00:20:41,764 --> 00:20:43,680
Damn it! It's a trap!

229
00:20:50,899 --> 00:20:56,740
How's that? Now you know how terrifying the Madam of X-Union is!

230
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,940
It was an X-Union trap!

231
00:21:00,493 --> 00:21:01,379
Again today!

232
00:21:01,540 --> 00:21:03,546
That's right.

233
00:21:24,576 --> 00:21:28,180
Curse those annoying brats! I have to bring the ceiling down fast, or else...

234
00:21:31,629 --> 00:21:33,160
Just you wait...

235
00:21:33,809 --> 00:21:35,160
Franz! Let's get out fast!

236
00:21:43,903 --> 00:21:44,646
Franz!

237
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:46,800
Alright, I did it!

238
00:22:25,214 --> 00:22:28,180
I'm sick and tired of pretending to be the fake Ribbon Knight!

239
00:22:29,099 --> 00:22:31,806
No, it was my fault for misunderstanding the Ribbon Knight.

240
00:22:33,049 --> 00:22:35,700
Also, pardon me, but I must return this to you.

241
00:22:36,849 --> 00:22:39,960
Oh, keep it as a token of thanks for saving us.

242
00:22:40,764 --> 00:22:43,025
My, such a wonderful gift?

243
00:22:43,110 --> 00:22:44,159
We couldn't possibly.

244
00:22:44,424 --> 00:22:47,980
Don't hesitate. Another agent from X-Union might show up anytime.

245
00:22:48,399 --> 00:22:50,820
Please keep it safe for when that time comes.

246
00:22:53,329 --> 00:22:54,680
I'm the one who got it!

247
00:22:54,814 --> 00:22:56,838
No, it was me, it was me!

248
00:22:56,862 --> 00:22:58,531
I'm the one who fetched this, me!

249
00:22:58,555 --> 00:23:01,700
You two shouldn't fight—you need to get along.

250
00:23:03,195 --> 00:23:03,968
Thanks.

251
00:23:03,993 --> 00:23:05,120
Sorry about that.

252
00:23:05,863 --> 00:23:08,711
Sapphire now, let's join forces and fight together as well.

253
00:23:08,735 --> 00:23:09,818
Right, Franz.

254
00:23:12,462 --> 00:23:14,462

